Description:
  Apple T1 / iBridge1,1 support in the USB layer:
  - Device table: adds iBridge1,1 / x619ap (CPID 0x8002, BDID 0x12), which all four Touch Bar Macs share.
  - String descriptors: the T1 in recovery often misses libusb's hard-coded 1 s timeout for the
    iSerialNumber read (LIBUSB_ERROR_TIMEOUT), losing the device identity and the AP/SEP nonces. Adds a
    retrying reader using libirecovery's own USB_TIMEOUT, and on Linux a fallback to the kernel's
    cached serial string from sysfs (matched by bus/devnum), used both when opening a device and in
    the hotplug add handler (which previously gave up and never emitted IRECV_DEVICE_ADD).
  - Only assume the legacy CPID 0x8900 when the iBoot string is non-empty but lacks CPID; an empty
    string means the read failed and must not mis-identify a modern part.
Regenerate:   git -C <checkout> -c diff.mnemonicPrefix=false diff HEAD   (base commit checked out, patch applied in the worktree)

